Your grace shal find him in your further co~fere~ce Graue, wise, courtly, & scholler like, vndersta~dingly read In the necessities of the life of man. He knowes that man is mortall by his birth; He knowes that men must dye, and therefore liue;
He knowes that man must liue, and therefore eate,
And if it shall please your grace, to accompany your selfe with him, I doubt not, but that hee will at the least, make good my commendations.
